.TH XD\-ACCESS 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-access \- Accessibility Options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-access
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SY xd\-access
.B \-\-shortcut
.I feature
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-access
is Windows XP's Accessibility Options (Control Panel):
.TP
.B Keyboard
StickyKeys, FilterKeys (SlowKeys and BounceKeys) and ToggleKeys, each with
its settings and XP's keyboard shortcut.
.TP
.B Sound
SoundSentry (a flash when a sound plays) and ShowSounds.
.TP
.B Display
High Contrast, the text cursor's blink rate, and the pointer's size.
.TP
.B Mouse
MouseKeys.
.TP
.B General
Turning the features off after a time idle, and the shortcuts' warnings
and sounds.
.PP
The settings go to
.IR desktop.ini ,
and
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
carries them out.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on tab
.IR n :
0 Keyboard, 1 Sound, 2 Display, 3 Mouse, 4 General.
.TP
.BI \-\-shortcut " feature"
The box asking whether to keep a feature that its keyboard shortcut has
just turned on (Cancel turns it off again):
.BR stickykeys ", " filterkeys ", " togglekeys " or " mousekeys .
The compositor runs this.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.BR [Accessibility] ,
and High Contrast's look in
.BR [Appearance] .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-compositor (1),
.BR xd\-control (1)
